# Everything that must not reach the build context.
#
# A .dockerignore is a security control, not an optimisation. Without it,
# COPY pulls in .env, .git and the local virtualenv - so the image would
# carry real secrets and the whole commit history, and `docker history`
# would show them to anyone who can pull it.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Version control ---
.git
.gitignore

# --- Local environments and caches ---
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache

# --- Things the image does not need ---
PROJECT_PLAN.md
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.github
nginx
*.md
!README.md
